have like some common DNA with Genghis Khan

00:02:49.286 --> 00:02:51.846
just because he sired soo many children

00:02:51.846 --> 00:02:54.993
So yes, House Stark can trace their lineage to the High King of the First Men

00:02:54.993 --> 00:02:56.704
but so can a lot of other people

00:02:56.704 --> 00:03:01.400
For example, on of his sons, Garth the Gardener, went on to find House Gardener

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:04.703
Obviously we know during Aegon’s Conquest of Westeros

00:03:04.703 --> 00:03:07.640
House Gardener fell, and House Tyrell kind of took their place

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:10.913
But the Starks in general just trace their lineage to the First Men

00:03:10.913 --> 00:03:15.062
Much more so than some of the other houses which trace their lineage more to the Andals

00:03:15.062 --> 00:03:18.698
Or say like the Martells in the South, who trace their lineage to the Rhoynar

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:22.889
The House Starks though, you know, much more than say some of the other great houses of Westeros

00:03:22.889 --> 00:03:25.934
trace their lineage to the First Men and the Children of the Forest

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:30.277
Most maesters in the Citadel believe though, that Garth was just like a war chief

00:03:30.277 --> 00:03:35.043
like a typical war chief, that led people across the Arm of Dorne into Westeros

