The First Men migrated to Westeros using the Arm of Dorne

00:03:38.586 --> 00:03:42.888
There’s a lot of argument as to who the first official leader of the First Men was

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:45.166
Mostly they just call him the First King

00:03:45.166 --> 00:03:47.779
That was about twelve thousand years before Aegon’s Conquest 

00:03:47.779 --> 00:03:51.096
so there’s no promise that George RR Martin is ever going to explore this

00:03:51.096 --> 00:03:56.900
Moving down the Stark line, it’s believed that one of Garth’s other sons, Bran the Bloody Blade

00:03:56.914 --> 00:03:59.234
was Brandon the Builder’s father.

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:01.566
The only thing of note that he is really credited with

00:04:01.566 --> 00:04:05.955
is driving the giants north of The Reach and driving out a lot of the Children of the Forest

00:04:05.955 --> 00:04:08.105
There’s a lot more that’s known about Bran the Builder

00:04:08.105 --> 00:04:10.850
but still a lot of the history that was recorded around his time

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:15.143
was written by maesters that lived thousands of years after he was alive

00:04:15.143 --> 00:04:17.326
So you know, you could view it some of it as conjecture

00:04:17.326 --> 00:04:20.769
But generally you know, he lived towards the end of the Age of Heroes

00:04:20.811 --> 00:04:25.691
The Age of Heroes began around the time the First Men signed a peace treaty 

00:04:25.691 --> 00:04:28.324
with the Children of the Forest and they stopped fighting each other.

00:04:28.324 --> 00:04:32.117
As part of the pact, the Children of the Forest just took to the forest

00:04:32.117 --> 00:04:34.144
