That’s why there's no Stark blade inside the Iron Throne

00:05:14.565 --> 00:05:19.230
Aegon the Conqueror only melted down the blades of people that refused to bend the knee

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.352
This is what the Iron Throne is really supposed to look like

00:05:21.352 --> 00:05:22.784
you know the show made it a lot smaller

00:05:22.784 --> 00:05:25.543
so you could see that there is a lot of people that did not bend the knee

00:05:25.543 --> 00:05:27.788
I know that there's a lot of confusion about that because they said that

00:05:27.788 --> 00:05:31.489
all of the former kings of Westeros had their blades melted down

00:05:31.489 --> 00:05:34.609
but technically in the books, it's only the kings that did not bend the knee

00:05:34.749 --> 00:05:36.349
when Aegon asked them to

00:05:36.349 --> 00:05:40.913
It was a situation where he was like, "You can either bend the knee, or I'll melt you with my dragons."

00:05:40.913 --> 00:05:44.730
So in and around the same time, Brandon the Builder's credited with building The Wall

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:45.640
or starting to build The Wall

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:48.330
He's also credited with starting to build Winterfell

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:50.266
